        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Māui es conocido en todo el Pacífico, y cada isla cuenta a su manera la historia del cielo.",
          "en": "Māui is known all across the Pacific, and every island tells the sky story its own way."
        },
        {
          "es": "En Samoa lo llaman Tiʻitiʻi. Dicen que apoyó los pies contra las rocas y empujó.",
          "en": "In Samoa, he is called Tiʻitiʻi. People say he braced his feet against rocks and pushed."
        },
        {
          "es": "En otro relato de Samoa, una mujer premia al que levanta el cielo con un trago de su cáscara de coco.",
          "en": "In another Samoan story, a woman rewards the man who lifts the sky with a drink from her coconut shell."
        },
        {
          "es": "En Manihiki, en las islas Cook, Māui y su padre Ru empujan el cielo desde dos lados.",
          "en": "On Manihiki, in the Cook Islands, Māui and his father Ru push the sky from two sides."
        },
        {
          "es": "Luego lo alisan con hachas de piedra, hasta dejarlo como una cúpula azul y limpia.",
          "en": "Then they smooth it with stone adzes, until it is a clean blue dome."
        }
      ],
